[
    {
        "content": "<p>i'm looking for an example in mathlib where a declaration (possibly even an instance) has an instance argument with a nested instance argument, i.e. something of the following pattern:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 586384355,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776621072
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(i'm looking for this because of a discussion on discord on the behaviour of instance arguments which are pi types)</p>",
        "id": 586384468,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776621186
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm pretty sure instance synthesis won't pick up on <code>[A a]</code> while synthesizing <code>[B a]</code></p>",
        "id": 586384529,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1776621255
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i think it will, actually...</p>",
        "id": 586384566,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776621285
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(I know because I tried to make something like this and it didn't work)</p>",
        "id": 586384584,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1776621299
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ah, you're right</p>",
        "id": 586384640,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776621359
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"kn\">opaque</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: failed to synthesize instance of type class</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  (a : X) → [A a] → B a</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Hint: Type class instance resolution failures can be inspected with the `set_option trace.Meta.synthInstance true` command.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 586384685,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776621388
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/example.20of.20nested.20instance-argument.20in.20mathlib/near/586384584\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(I know because I tried to make something like this and it didn't work)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>see <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Instance.20hypotheses.20in.20instance.20parameter/near/512706663\">#lean4 &gt; Instance hypotheses in instance parameter @ 💬</a></p>",
        "id": 586385189,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1776621751
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This code works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"kn\">opaque</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 586390580,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1776626385
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>right... it is, however, mathematically different.</p>",
        "id": 586390667,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776626448
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But I think your <code>[∀ a : R, [A a] → B a]</code> is very misleading. Suppose <code>A a</code> never holds. Then <code>[∀ a : R, [A a] → B a]</code> is true. I don't think there are any meaningful results take this as an assumption.</p>",
        "id": 586390690,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1776626465
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>[∀ a : R, [A a] → B a]</code> is equivalent to say \"for all <code>a : R</code>, either <code>A a</code> does not hold, or <code>B a</code> holds\". I think asserting some instance does not exist (your <code>A a</code>) cannot be an instance.</p>",
        "id": 586390881,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1776626631
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i think it can happen? right now i'm thinking of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsReduced#doc\">docs#IsReduced</a>, which says that nilpotent elements of a ring (or more general) are equal to zero</p>",
        "id": 586391032,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776626807
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>of course equality is not a class in lean, but a) it could be in theory (although the ergonomics would probably not be improved by that), and b) the fact that a situation this close to my question exists makes it plausible that a situation matching my question exists too.</p>",
        "id": 586391151,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776626919
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>of course, arguably the fact that this doesn't currently work is a bug</p>",
        "id": 586392440,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776628088
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"366779\">Jz Pan</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/example.20of.20nested.20instance-argument.20in.20mathlib/near/586390881\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>[∀ a : R, [A a] → B a]</code> is equivalent to say \"for all <code>a : R</code>, either <code>A a</code> does not hold, or <code>B a</code> holds\". I think asserting some instance does not exist (your <code>A a</code>) cannot be an instance.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Since <code>A a</code> and <code>B a</code> could also be data I don't think that's a valid substitution to make.</p>",
        "id": 586393386,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1776628976
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's even more subtle if <code>A a</code> and <code>B a</code> are data; in this case the <code>[∀ a : R, [A a] → B a]</code> means that for each <code>a</code>, a map <code>A a → B a</code> is given, different choices of maps potentially give different definition of <code>foo</code>. So in this case I think the only reasonable way is define a new structure class with one field which is <code>∀ a : R, [A a] → B a</code>. IMO we cannot think <code>∀ a : R, [A a] → B a</code> simply as an instance of <code>B</code>.</p>",
        "id": 587674335,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1776661441
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"366779\">Jz Pan</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/example.20of.20nested.20instance-argument.20in.20mathlib/near/587674335\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>for each <code>a</code>, a map <code>A a → B a</code> is given, different choices of maps potentially give different definition of <code>foo</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Isn't this always the case? Even if I just have <code>[B bar]</code>, that means that a value of <code>B bar</code> is given, with different choices of <code>B bar</code> potentially giving different definitions of <code>foo</code>. The point of typeclass is that there is some canonical choice that we want to pick.</p>",
        "id": 587726390,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1776679688
    }
]